  </table>
  <p class="muted">MCQs and Long Questions are structurally fixed in this dataset: MCQs appear exactly {mcq_counts[0]} times in every present year and Long Questions exactly {long_counts[0]} times in every present year. Short Questions are the variable component, ranging from {min(short_counts)} to {max(short_counts)} per year.</p>
</section>

<section id="yearly-distribution">
  <h2>Year-by-Year Question Volume Analysis</h2>
  <p>Question volume is not random: it follows three clear phases. The earliest phase, 2015–2016, contains <strong>27 questions per year</strong>. The 2017–2019 phase rises to <strong>36 questions per year</strong>, driven entirely by an increase in Short Questions. From 2021–2025, the structure settles at <strong>33 questions per year</strong>. Because 2020 is absent, the change from 2019 to 2021 should be interpreted as the next available-year comparison, not necessarily a direct calendar-year shift.</p>
  <div class="chart"><div class="chart-title">Total Questions per Present Year</div>{svg_line_chart([(y, year_totals[y]) for y in present_years])}</div>
