  </table>
  <div class="callout warning"><strong>Important interpretation:</strong> the largest observed increase is from 2016 to 2017, where total questions rise by 9 ({(9/27*100):.1f}%). The only observed decrease is from 2019 to 2021, where total questions fall by 3 ({(-3/36*100):.1f}%) against the previous present year. No value for 2020 can be inferred from the dataset.</div>
</section>

<section id="question-type-analysis">
  <h2>Question Type Composition & Trends</h2>
  <p>The exam structure is stable in two dimensions and variable in one. <strong>MCQs remain constant at 15 per present year</strong>, while <strong>Long Questions remain constant at 3 per present year</strong>. The overall volume changes come from <strong>Short Questions</strong>: 9 in 2015–2016, 18 in 2017–2019, and 15 in 2021–2025.</p>
  <div class="chart"><div class="chart-title">Question-Type Ratio by Year</div>{svg_stacked_bars(present_years, percent=True)}</div>
  <div class="grid two-col">
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Stable Components</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>MCQs:</strong> {overall_type['MCQs']} total, {pct(shares_overall['MCQs'])} overall share, exactly 15 every present year.</li>
        <li><strong>Long Questions:</strong> {overall_type['Long']} total, {pct(shares_overall['Long'])} overall share, exactly 3 every present year.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Variable Component</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Short Questions:</strong> {overall_type['Short']} total, {pct(shares_overall['Short'])} overall share.</li>
        <li>Short Questions double from 9 to 18 between the 2015–2016 and 2017–2019 phases, then settle at 15 from 2021 onward.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p>Educators should therefore treat the exam as structurally stable in its MCQ and Long Question anchors, but responsive in the Short Question section. Short-answer preparation deserves special planning because it is the section most associated with year-to-year volume change.</p>
</section>

<section id="topic-patterns">
  <h2>Recurring Topics & Question Content Patterns</h2>
  <p>Keyword analysis was performed on the <code>question</code> column after replacing the <code>$</code> delimiter with spaces, lowercasing text, removing common instruction words, and grouping simple plural forms. Counts below are direct token or phrase counts from the dataset; topic-category counts are question-level hits and can overlap when a question contains multiple topic families.</p>
